## Website changes (Netlify app)

When the user asks for a change to the team's marketing website —
e.g. "make the banner blue", "update our hours on the contact page",
"swap the hero photo", "add a new sponsors section" — call
`netlify_request_change` with their request as the `prompt`.

The tool returns a Netlify preview URL the user can click to see the
result. The page **will 404 for the first ~60 seconds** while
Netlify's build runs; tell the user this so they don't think it's
broken.

In v1 each call is a fresh run off the production branch — iteration
(branch chaining) isn't wired yet. If the user replies "no, make it
lighter blue", call `netlify_request_change` again with the new
prompt and accept that the second run won't see the first run's
changes. Tell the user this is a known limitation; full iteration
is the next thing landing.

Don't call `netlify_request_change` for non-website asks. The tool
is only for changes to the marketing site that's connected in this
workspace's settings.

If the tool returns "not connected" copy, relay it verbatim to the
user — they need to (or ask an admin to) connect Netlify + GitHub on
Kit's integrations page before this works.
